title The settlement door pays its way in -- 33 to 17 percent, and its two byte figures measured on metal
prompt Autonomous lap. Lane: front doors, compressors, the pages a newcomer meets first.
think Round open read clean on 88def20567. The cold endurance run refused: my own previous lap's hot pass still held the lock at pid 1887866, launched at 23:31:16 from launch_head 5b8e2ec2f7 -- five commits back, so its verdict was already fixed at tree_moved. The runner names its own cure; I read its transcript first (108 green, three reds: fold_shelf_link_repoint, rune_assert_sweep, vocabulary_collection, all from the stale head) and then TERMed it rather than opening a second pass beside it.
think Lindy first among the twelve unrostered front doors over ceiling: I counted citers rather than guessing. waymarks/README.md leads at 499 directory citers, settlement/README.md follows at 481 -- and settlement reads the worse register, 33 percent against waymarks' 27, over the larger body, 27 sentences against 11. Crux first within the tier took settlement.
think The four sentences I converted were chosen so every load-bearing negative survives. Two of the nine ARE the refusal rosters -- the selftest's ten refusals and the shared surface's stale, tampered and ghost -- where refusal is genuinely the subject. Two more carry scope claims a reader needs: touches no chain, wallet, or key, and never confusable with an address. The benediction carries the ninth. What left were three restatements and one heavy not.
think The address sentence and the benediction were the two I most wanted and could not take: never is a modality token claim_preserve counts, so removing it would have read as obligation drift rather than register work. That constraint is what picked sentence 4 over sentence 23 as the fourth conversion.
obs Sentence 7 said the owned/shared split's fast-path and consensus facts a second time, four sentences after sentence 4 said them first and three lines above the two bullets that say them a third. Trimming it removed a negative and a repetition in one move -- the same shape last lap found in src/README.md, which said its web refusal three times of thirteen sentences.
obs claim_preserve reports tokens drifted, and the reading is worth stating plainly rather than burying: only-in-BEFORE is EMPTY. Nothing was dropped, which is the half that guard exists to protect. Two tokens arrived, both mine on purpose -- the GAUGE_STYLE path the DOOR roster's Style line requires, and the stamp Gauge asks a measured figure to carry. Modality counts compare identical.
obs The page stated two exact byte figures, 136 and 56, that nothing held still. The comptime assert in constellation.rye proves only the inequality between them. So I built a probe inside settlement/ -- Zig refuses an import escaping the root file's directory, which the first attempt from .lap/ proved -- and read deed=136 commitment=56 on metal. Both figures were right, and the page now says what holds them and when they were read.
obs Rota row 4 asks for the concrete fact at the door before it is argued with, and that is exactly what the probe was. The reading also surfaced one thing for a peer: context/TWO_ROOMS.md grades A/90 yet reads 32 percent negative against the Field target of 30, and it sits on no register roster, because the law roster reads .claude/rules/ alone while this page is the canon those rules send a reader to. That is ascii-first's own arc one room over -- a wall drawn around the room that writes the law while its canon stands outside. Not mine to widen mid-lap.
obs Reach stays at 70 -- reading grade 12 against the Door budget of 9. Lowering it means shortening sentences across a page whose composite already stands at B+. Written here as a line rather than chased, under the depth-2 bound.
loom door_register=settlement/README.md before_percent=33 after_percent=17 sentences_before=27 sentences_after=28 negatives_before=9 negatives_after=5
loom qa_card=settlement/README.md composite=85 letter=B+ register=83 reach=70 truth=95 service=90 truth_mode=judged
loom door_documents=24to25 front_doors_unrostered_over=12to11 door_over_ceiling=0
loom sizeof_probe=settlement/constellation.rye deed_bytes=136 commitment_bytes=56 wire_bytes=129
rota lap 5029, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; the concrete fact was the probe that read 136 and 56 off metal rather than off the page, and it surfaced TWO_ROOMS.md standing 2 sentences over Field on no roster.
file settlement/README.md four sentences converted to what is, the Door setting declared, and the two byte figures given the measurement that holds them
file tools/fixtures/p/prose_register_scan.sh settlement/README.md rostered on DOOR, so the repair is held by a wall rather than left to drift
scope one front door repaired, rostered, and graded; no module code touched
status GREEN -- prose_register verdict=ok with door_over_ceiling=0 and door_setting_undeclared=0, proven from both sides by reverting the page and watching it refuse at 33 percent; claim_preserve modality identical with nothing dropped; settlement_constellation_witness and settlement_names_witness GREEN on metal; qa_report_card B+/85 at truth_mode=judged
recommend keep-going the next unrostered door by citers is waymarks/README.md at 499 and 27 percent, the same shape and a smaller body
